From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haven Maintainers <maintainers@haven.sh>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] monitor: report host-owned files as 0:0 while elevated
 under --setuid-root

Under `--fake-id=1000:1000 --setuid-root --setgid-root`, executing a
`04755` setuid binary such as `/usr/bin/sudo` elevates `euid` and `suid`
to `0`, but `sudo` immediately validates that `/etc/sudo.conf`,
`/etc/sudoers`, `/etc/sudoers.d/*`, and `sudoers.so` are owned by UID 0
(sometimes after temporarily toggling `euid` via `seteuid(ruid)` while
keeping `suid == 0`). Because Android extracts the entire guest rootfs
under a single unprivileged app UID, remapping `cng_g_host_uid` to fixed
`cng_g_fake_uid` (1000) even when elevated causes `sudo` to abort with
`/etc/sudo.conf is owned by uid 1000, should be 0`.

Match PRoot `fake_id0`'s `suid`-aware stat remap: while the live
synthetic credential set holds root (`euid == 0 || suid == 0`), remap
`cng_g_host_uid`/`cng_g_host_gid` to `0`; unprivileged processes
(`euid != 0 && suid != 0`, e.g. Sway checking `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` or OpenSSH
checking `~/.ssh/config`) continue to see `cng_g_fake_uid`/`cng_g_fake_gid`.
---
 include/cng/monitor.h | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/cng/monitor.h b/include/cng/monitor.h
index 2436c2e..7d491cc 100644
--- a/include/cng/monitor.h
+++ b/include/cng/monitor.h
@@ -180,10 +180,22 @@ int cng_fake_root(void);
  * user is shown as owned by the fake id; every other owner passes through. A
  * no-op unless a fake identity is active. */
 static inline unsigned cng_remap_uid(unsigned u) {
-    return (cng_g_fake_id && u == cng_g_host_uid) ? cng_g_fake_uid : u;
+    if (!cng_g_fake_id || u != cng_g_host_uid)
+        return u;
+    if (cng_g_fake_uid == 0)
+        return 0;
+    struct cng_cred_ids id;
+    cng_cred_ids(&id);
+    return (id.euid == 0 || id.suid == 0) ? 0 : cng_g_fake_uid;
 }
 static inline unsigned cng_remap_gid(unsigned g) {
-    return (cng_g_fake_id && g == cng_g_host_gid) ? cng_g_fake_gid : g;
+    if (!cng_g_fake_id || g != cng_g_host_gid)
+        return g;
+    if (cng_g_fake_gid == 0)
+        return 0;
+    struct cng_cred_ids id;
+    cng_cred_ids(&id);
+    return (id.egid == 0 || id.sgid == 0 || id.euid == 0 || id.suid == 0) ? 0 : cng_g_fake_gid;
 }
 
 /* Visible owner/group of a file with mode `mode`: a setuid/setgid *regular* file
